        ('A2 note, 2026-10-19, X8/X8v','Resample ablation (g from a random other jet) changes 27.9 % of calls; mean ablation 14.9 %; unit ranking Spearman 0.965 between the two.'),
        ('refinement 7, 2026-10-20, X9w/X9wv, E24/E24v', 'PFN, EFN and Deep Sets trained with random translations up to 0.08 rad do not respond to such translations (W → Z ≤ 0.012 vs 0.35–0.71, seed-level p 0.0093) but do beyond them (0.12 rad: 0.51–0.84): new claim A10r (0.55); X9w\'s "mass about the jet\'s own centroid" refuted; JEDI-linear HGQ-50 aug unresolved. Azimuth scramble at fixed moments: radial S objects ≤ 0.19 sd, excess through S58/S31; call share equals a τ21 classifier\'s and Deep Sets / PFN: new claims A3z (0.6), A13 (0.5). A3, A10m unchanged.'),
        ('refinement 8, 2026-10-20, X9x/X9xv, E24w/E24wv', 'Augmentation range scan (A 0.04–0.30 rad, PFN, EFN, Deep Sets): the tolerated translation follows A (break slope 0.89–1.04, r ≥ 0.993); beyond A calls move heavier. A10r reworded (v1 kept in the claim), 0.55 → 0.75. New A10c (0.45): in Deep Sets and EFN part of the tolerance uses a 2-dim linear centroid read-out; X9x\'s "no signed offset variable used" superseded. Two-prong jets at matched mass: scattering vs rotating the soft prong intact gives the same call change in JEDI-linear on three samples (D − P −0.28 to −0.53, τ21 classifiers +3.5 to +4.3); moving the prong works through g. A13 reworded (v1 kept), 0.5 → 0.6. S58/S31 not named by pooled half-plane fits (R² ≤ 0.19); A3z 0.6 (=).'),
        ('refinement 9, 2026-10-20, E25/E25v, E24x/E24xv, E23w/E23wv', 'Official 16-feature JEDI-linear: zero first-layer weight on Δη, Δφ, η, φ; angles enter through ΔR (often with pT in the same cut); radial objects come from the input; the 0.06 rad translation W → Z 0.48–0.49 via ΔR, following Σ pT ΔR². The program is shared at the level of the observable, not the circuit; new A1f (0.75), A4 0.93, A10m 0.87, A1x scope stated (3-feature checkpoints). S58/S31 named: no per-particle input, thresholds follow fixed-frame count dipole (S31) / quadrupole (S58) sums, R² 0.93–0.95; the 180° rotation response of S58 is not explained by the quadrupole name; new A3c (0.65). E23w\'s two-gain pattern is an estimator property (IV: S 0.77, h4–z 0.86–0.97); odd response follows the unweighted centroid (16–35 %) more than M1 (2–4 %); A4n reworded (v1 kept), 0.6 → 0.5; product test null within a wide band, product 0.25 → 0.2.'),
